-- R01 Short Functional Texts: Batch 3
-- 13 A2, 15 B1, 15 B2. Completes 30 questions per level when combined with previous batches.
-- Original items informed by public CEFR exam task descriptions; no Cambridge text copied.
-- All questions test English reading only; no arithmetic or mathematical reasoning.
begin;
insert into public.reading_question_bank
(question_code,category,cefr_level,topic,skill,passage,prompt,options,correct_option,rationale,difficulty,estimated_seconds,status)
values
('A2-031','R01','A2','Education and Learning','Identifying purpose','ART ROOM NOTICE
The art room will be closed after lunch today while the walls are painted. Students who need materials for their projects should collect them before 11 a.m.','When should students collect their materials?','[{"label":"A","text":"After lunch today."},{"label":"B","text":"Before 11 a.m."},{"label":"C","text":"Tomorrow morning."},{"label":"D","text":"When the painting is finished."}]'::jsonb,'B','The notice asks students to collect materials before 11 a.m.','core',40,'draft'),
('A2-032','R01','A2','Transportation and Travel','Understanding a message','TEXT FROM MAY
I''m already at the bus stop, but the road is very busy. The bus is moving slowly, so I may arrive a little late. Please wait for me near the entrance.','Why might May be late?','[{"label":"A","text":"She missed the bus yesterday."},{"label":"B","text":"She is waiting at the wrong entrance."},{"label":"C","text":"The bus is delayed by traffic."},{"label":"D","text":"She has decided to walk home."}]'::jsonb,'C','May says the bus is moving slowly because the road is busy.','core',45,'draft'),
('A2-033','R01','A2','Food Production','Understanding instructions','MARKET STALL
Please taste the fruit samples before choosing what to buy. The samples are free, but customers should use the small paper cups provided. Please do not touch the fruit on display.','What should customers use for tasting?','[{"label":"A","text":"The paper cups."},{"label":"B","text":"Their own bags."},{"label":"C","text":"The fruit display."},{"label":"D","text":"The large serving plates."}]'::jsonb,'A','The notice tells customers to use the small paper cups.','core',40,'draft'),
('A2-034','R01','A2','Sports and Health','Understanding a rule','SWIMMING POOL
Children under 12 must be accompanied by an adult. All swimmers must shower before entering the pool. Food and glass bottles are not allowed in the pool area.','What must every swimmer do?','[{"label":"A","text":"Bring an adult."},{"label":"B","text":"Wear a swimming cap."},{"label":"C","text":"Shower before swimming."},{"label":"D","text":"Leave their shoes outside."}]'::jsonb,'C','The shower rule applies to all swimmers.','core',45,'draft'),
('A2-035','R01','A2','Technology and Society','Understanding a message','EMAIL FROM THE IT TEAM
The school Wi-Fi password has changed. The new password is on the noticeboard outside the computer room. Please do not share it with visitors.','Where can students find the new password?','[{"label":"A","text":"In their school email."},{"label":"B","text":"On the noticeboard near the computer room."},{"label":"C","text":"At the school reception desk."},{"label":"D","text":"On the classroom door."}]'::jsonb,'B','The email directs students to the noticeboard outside the computer room.','core',40,'draft'),
('A2-036','R01','A2','Cities and Housing','Understanding a condition','RENTAL ROOM NOTICE
The room is available from the beginning of next month. It includes a desk and wardrobe, but tenants need to bring their own bedding. The building has a shared laundry room.','What should a new tenant bring?','[{"label":"A","text":"A desk and wardrobe."},{"label":"B","text":"A washing machine."},{"label":"C","text":"Their own bedding."},{"label":"D","text":"A new door key."}]'::jsonb,'C','The notice says bedding is not provided.','core',45,'draft'),
('A2-037','R01','A2','Environment and Pollution','Understanding a request','SCHOOL GARDEN
Please do not pick flowers from the front garden. The gardening club uses them to attract butterflies and other insects. Visitors are welcome to take photographs from the path.','What are visitors asked not to do?','[{"label":"A","text":"Take photographs."},{"label":"B","text":"Walk along the path."},{"label":"C","text":"Pick the flowers."},{"label":"D","text":"Look for butterflies."}]'::jsonb,'C','The notice asks visitors not to pick flowers.','core',40,'draft'),
('A2-038','R01','A2','Consumer Economics','Understanding a message','CUSTOMER EMAIL
Thank you for your order. One item is currently unavailable, so we have sent the other products today. We will email you again when the missing item is ready to be sent.','What has happened to the order?','[{"label":"A","text":"Nothing has been sent yet."},{"label":"B","text":"All the items arrived together."},{"label":"C","text":"The customer must collect every item."},{"label":"D","text":"Most items have been sent, but one is delayed."}]'::jsonb,'D','The email explains that the available items were sent and one will follow later.','core',50,'draft'),
('A2-039','R01','A2','Media and Youth','Identifying purpose','SCHOOL RADIO
Would you like to choose the music for Friday''s lunchtime programme? Send your song suggestions to the radio club by Thursday. Please include the name of the artist.','What does the radio club want students to send?','[{"label":"A","text":"Ideas for songs to play."},{"label":"B","text":"Recordings of Friday''s programme."},{"label":"C","text":"A list of their favourite artists only."},{"label":"D","text":"Permission to miss lunchtime."}]'::jsonb,'A','Students are invited to send song suggestions and artist names.','core',40,'draft'),
('A2-040','R01','A2','Climate and Weather','Understanding advice','HIKING GROUP MESSAGE
The path near the waterfall is slippery after last night''s rain. We will use the lower forest route instead. Please wear shoes with a good grip.','Why has the group changed its route?','[{"label":"A","text":"The waterfall is closed permanently."},{"label":"B","text":"The original path may be unsafe."},{"label":"C","text":"The forest route is shorter."},{"label":"D","text":"The group wants to avoid the rain."}]'::jsonb,'B','The path is slippery, so the group chooses a safer route.','core',45,'draft'),
('A2-041','R01','A2','Health and Nutrition','Understanding a warning','FOOD LABEL
Keep this product in the refrigerator after opening. Use within three days. Do not eat if the seal is broken when you first open the package.','When should someone avoid eating the product?','[{"label":"A","text":"When it has been in the refrigerator."},{"label":"B","text":"When it is opened for the first time."},{"label":"C","text":"When the seal is already broken."},{"label":"D","text":"When it is used within three days."}]'::jsonb,'C','The label warns customers not to eat it if the seal is broken on opening.','core',45,'draft'),
('A2-042','R01','A2','Space Exploration','Understanding a message','PLANETARIUM TICKETS
Today''s 2 p.m. show is full. A few seats are still available for the 4 p.m. show. Please ask at the information desk if you would like to change your booking.','What can visitors do if they cannot attend the 2 p.m. show?','[{"label":"A","text":"Watch the show without a ticket."},{"label":"B","text":"Ask to change to the later show."},{"label":"C","text":"Wait until the planetarium closes."},{"label":"D","text":"Book a show at another museum."}]'::jsonb,'B','The notice offers a change to the 4 p.m. show, subject to available seats.','core',45,'draft'),
('A2-043','R01','A2','Energy and Electricity','Understanding instructions','COMPUTER ROOM
Please save your work before logging out. Headphones must be returned to the labelled box. Leave the keyboards on the desks for the next class.','What should students return?','[{"label":"A","text":"The keyboards."},{"label":"B","text":"Their saved work."},{"label":"C","text":"The headphones."},{"label":"D","text":"The computer desks."}]'::jsonb,'C','The instructions say headphones should be returned to the labelled box.','core',40,'draft'),
('B1-031','R01','B1','Media and Youth','Understanding intention','MESSAGE FROM THE SCHOOL EDITOR
Thanks for sending your article about the sports festival. The information is useful, but readers who were not there may find it difficult to follow. Could you add a short introduction explaining what the event was and why it was organised?','What does the editor want the writer to do?','[{"label":"A","text":"Remove the details about the festival."},{"label":"B","text":"Add background information for readers."},{"label":"C","text":"Change the article into an interview."},{"label":"D","text":"Submit the article to a different magazine."}]'::jsonb,'B','The editor wants an introduction that helps readers understand the event.','core',60,'draft'),
('B1-032','R01','B1','Technology and Society','Understanding implication','APP UPDATE NOTICE
The latest version allows users to download lessons for offline use. Your saved lessons will remain available without an internet connection, although new comments and updates will appear only when you reconnect.','What can users do without internet access?','[{"label":"A","text":"Download new comments from teachers."},{"label":"B","text":"Receive every new update immediately."},{"label":"C","text":"Open lessons they have already saved."},{"label":"D","text":"Create an account without registering."}]'::jsonb,'C','Saved lessons can be accessed offline; new comments and updates require reconnection.','core',60,'draft'),
('B1-033','R01','B1','Environment and Pollution','Understanding purpose','NEIGHBOURHOOD NOTICE
The council is considering replacing several roadside bins with larger recycling points. Before making a decision, it wants to know whether residents would find the new locations convenient. Please complete the short survey on the council website.','Why is the council asking residents to complete a survey?','[{"label":"A","text":"To find out what residents think about the proposed locations."},{"label":"B","text":"To announce that the bins have already been removed."},{"label":"C","text":"To ask residents to collect rubbish from the streets."},{"label":"D","text":"To explain how to build a recycling centre."}]'::jsonb,'A','The council is gathering opinions before deciding whether to change the bin locations.','core',65,'draft'),
('B1-034','R01','B1','College and Career Paths','Understanding suitability','VOLUNTEER OPPORTUNITY
The town museum needs weekend volunteers to welcome visitors and help with simple activities for children. Volunteers should be friendly and comfortable speaking to different people. Training will be provided, so previous museum experience is not necessary.','Who would be suitable for this role?','[{"label":"A","text":"Someone who can work only on weekday mornings."},{"label":"B","text":"Someone who prefers not to speak to visitors."},{"label":"C","text":"Someone who enjoys meeting people and can volunteer at weekends."},{"label":"D","text":"Someone who has to manage the museum alone."}]'::jsonb,'C','The role requires weekend availability and confidence speaking with visitors; training is provided.','core',65,'draft'),
('B1-035','R01','B1','Education and Learning','Understanding an opinion','STUDENT BLOG
I used to highlight almost every sentence in my textbook because it made me feel that I was studying. Later, I realised I remembered very little. Now I write a few questions after each section and try to answer them without looking. It takes more effort, but I can see what I actually understand.','What has the writer learned about studying?','[{"label":"A","text":"Highlighting every sentence guarantees good results."},{"label":"B","text":"Testing yourself can show what you really understand."},{"label":"C","text":"Reading a section once is always enough."},{"label":"D","text":"Studying should never require much effort."}]'::jsonb,'B','The writer now uses self-questioning to check understanding rather than relying on highlighting.','core',70,'draft'),
('B1-036','R01','B1','Health and Nutrition','Understanding a qualification','COMMUNITY COOKING COURSE
The course introduces simple ways to prepare balanced meals using ingredients that are easy to find locally. It is designed for beginners and does not require special equipment. Participants will prepare dishes together, but the course is not intended to provide professional cooking qualifications.','What should participants expect?','[{"label":"A","text":"A beginner-friendly course focused on practical cooking."},{"label":"B","text":"Advanced training for professional chefs."},{"label":"C","text":"A course that provides restaurant employment."},{"label":"D","text":"Lessons that require expensive kitchen equipment."}]'::jsonb,'A','The description emphasises beginner-level practical cooking and ordinary equipment.','core',65,'draft'),
('B1-037','R01','B1','Transportation and Travel','Understanding a message','RAIL SERVICE UPDATE
Trains are running normally between Central Station and the airport. Services in the opposite direction are delayed because of maintenance work. Passengers travelling from the airport should allow extra time for their journey.','Which passengers are most likely to be delayed?','[{"label":"A","text":"Those travelling from Central Station to the airport."},{"label":"B","text":"Those who have already bought a ticket."},{"label":"C","text":"Those travelling from the airport towards Central Station."},{"label":"D","text":"Those using the airport car park."}]'::jsonb,'C','The update says services from the airport are delayed.','core',60,'draft'),
('B1-038','R01','B1','Cities and Housing','Understanding a request','EMAIL TO PROPERTY MANAGER
Thank you for arranging the repair to the kitchen tap. The leak has stopped, but the cupboard underneath is still damp and has an unpleasant smell. Could someone check whether water has collected behind the unit?','What further help does the writer request?','[{"label":"A","text":"A replacement kitchen."},{"label":"B","text":"A check for water behind the cupboard."},{"label":"C","text":"A different repair appointment for the tap."},{"label":"D","text":"Permission to remove the kitchen sink."}]'::jsonb,'B','The writer asks for an inspection because dampness and a smell remain after the tap repair.','core',65,'draft'),
('B1-039','R01','B1','Sports and Health','Understanding advice','CLUB NEWSLETTER
Several members have asked whether they should train harder when they miss a session. Coaches recommend returning to the normal programme instead. Trying to make up every missed workout can lead to tiredness and reduce the quality of later sessions.','What do the coaches recommend?','[{"label":"A","text":"Doing extra sessions immediately."},{"label":"B","text":"Stopping training for the rest of the week."},{"label":"C","text":"Returning to the usual training plan."},{"label":"D","text":"Training harder before every missed session."}]'::jsonb,'C','The coaches advise members to resume the normal programme rather than overcompensate.','core',65,'draft'),
('B1-040','R01','B1','Food Production','Understanding a process','FARM VISIT INFORMATION
Visitors will first see how vegetables are grown in the greenhouse. The guide will then explain how produce is cleaned and packed before delivery. Please wear closed shoes, as some paths may be wet.','What will visitors learn about after seeing the greenhouse?','[{"label":"A","text":"How vegetables are cleaned and prepared for delivery."},{"label":"B","text":"How to sell vegetables in the town market."},{"label":"C","text":"How to repair the greenhouse roof."},{"label":"D","text":"How to cook the vegetables at home."}]'::jsonb,'A','The programme moves from growing vegetables to cleaning and packing them.','core',60,'draft'),
('B1-041','R01','B1','Artificial Intelligence','Understanding a recommendation','TEACHER''S NOTE ABOUT AI
An AI writing assistant can suggest clearer ways to express an idea. However, students should not accept every suggested change automatically. Sometimes the original sentence better reflects what the writer wants to say, especially when the tool misunderstands the context.','What does the teacher recommend?','[{"label":"A","text":"Accepting all AI suggestions to improve accuracy."},{"label":"B","text":"Using AI only when writing longer essays."},{"label":"C","text":"Choosing suggestions carefully and considering the intended meaning."},{"label":"D","text":"Avoiding all tools that offer writing feedback."}]'::jsonb,'C','The teacher advises students to judge suggestions in context rather than accept them automatically.','core',70,'draft'),
('B1-042','R01','B1','Climate and Weather','Understanding a warning','MOUNTAIN VISITOR CENTRE
The upper walking trail is open, but strong winds are expected later today. Visitors planning to use it should speak to staff before setting out. The lower trail is sheltered and remains suitable for most walkers.','What should visitors planning to use the upper trail do?','[{"label":"A","text":"Ignore the weather report."},{"label":"B","text":"Ask staff for advice before starting."},{"label":"C","text":"Use the trail after the visitor centre closes."},{"label":"D","text":"Take the lower trail only if they are experienced."}]'::jsonb,'B','The notice specifically asks upper-trail visitors to speak to staff before setting out.','core',65,'draft'),
('B1-043','R01','B1','Energy and Electricity','Understanding purpose','SCHOOL ENERGY PROJECT
The student team has placed reminder cards beside light switches in several classrooms. The cards are part of a project to find out whether simple changes in everyday behaviour can reduce unnecessary electricity use.','Why have the reminder cards been placed there?','[{"label":"A","text":"To advertise new classroom equipment."},{"label":"B","text":"To explain how electricity is generated."},{"label":"C","text":"To encourage people to switch off unused lights."},{"label":"D","text":"To tell students when the classrooms are closed."}]'::jsonb,'C','The cards are intended to encourage behaviour that reduces unnecessary electricity use.','core',60,'draft'),
('B1-044','R01','B1','Consumer Economics','Understanding a condition','ONLINE ORDER INFORMATION
Customers may cancel an order while its status is shown as ''Processing''. Once the parcel has been handed to the delivery company, cancellation is no longer possible. Customers can then follow the delivery instructions to request a return.','When can a customer cancel an order?','[{"label":"A","text":"Before it has been handed to the delivery company."},{"label":"B","text":"At any time after it has arrived."},{"label":"C","text":"Only after requesting a return."},{"label":"D","text":"When the delivery company has lost it."}]'::jsonb,'A','Cancellation is possible while the order is still processing, before dispatch to the delivery company.','core',65,'draft'),
('B1-045','R01','B1','Space Exploration','Understanding a contrast','MUSEUM REVIEW
The new space gallery contains fewer large models than the previous exhibition. Instead, it uses interactive screens to explain how satellites collect information about Earth. Some visitors may miss the impressive displays, but the new approach makes the science easier to explore.','What does the reviewer suggest about the new gallery?','[{"label":"A","text":"It is less informative because it has fewer models."},{"label":"B","text":"It focuses mainly on the history of museum design."},{"label":"C","text":"It offers a more interactive way to understand satellite science."},{"label":"D","text":"It is intended only for visitors with technical knowledge."}]'::jsonb,'C','The reviewer contrasts fewer models with interactive explanations that make the science easier to explore.','core',70,'draft'),
('B2-031','R01','B2','Media and Youth','Understanding implication','EDITORIAL GUIDELINES
The student magazine welcomes criticism of school policies, provided that submissions distinguish between evidence and personal opinion. Writers are not expected to agree with the editorial team, but they should represent opposing views fairly and avoid presenting rumours as established facts.','What freedom do contributors have?','[{"label":"A","text":"They may criticise school policies if they argue responsibly."},{"label":"B","text":"They must support the editorial team''s position."},{"label":"C","text":"They may publish rumours if the topic is important."},{"label":"D","text":"They should avoid mentioning opposing opinions."}]'::jsonb,'A','The guidelines allow criticism but require evidence, fairness and a clear distinction between fact and opinion.','core',80,'draft'),
('B2-032','R01','B2','Technology and Society','Understanding a qualification','DIGITAL LEARNING REVIEW
The platform''s analytics provide teachers with a useful overview of student activity. Yet frequent log-ins should not be treated as evidence of meaningful learning. A student may spend considerable time online without engaging deeply with the material, while another may work effectively in shorter sessions.','What caution does the reviewer make?','[{"label":"A","text":"Online activity figures should not be confused with actual learning."},{"label":"B","text":"Students should be required to remain online longer."},{"label":"C","text":"Short study sessions are always more effective."},{"label":"D","text":"Teachers should stop using digital learning platforms."}]'::jsonb,'A','The reviewer distinguishes measurable platform activity from genuine engagement and learning.','core',80,'draft'),
('B2-033','R01','B2','Environment and Pollution','Understanding an argument','CITY TREE-PLANTING PLAN
The proposal prioritises streets with little shade and high pedestrian use. Some residents have questioned why trees are not distributed evenly across every district. The planning team argues that concentrating early efforts where heat exposure is greatest will provide the most immediate public benefit, while later phases can extend coverage.','Why does the plan prioritise certain streets?','[{"label":"A","text":"To make every district receive exactly the same number of trees."},{"label":"B","text":"To avoid planting trees near busy roads."},{"label":"C","text":"To provide the greatest immediate benefit where heat exposure is high."},{"label":"D","text":"To complete the entire project in one phase."}]'::jsonb,'C','The plan targets areas with greater heat exposure and pedestrian use to maximise immediate benefit.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-034','R01','B2','College and Career Paths','Understanding stance','CAREER ADVICE COLUMN
Employers often describe adaptability as an essential quality. This should not be interpreted as a willingness to accept every change without question. Rather, adaptable employees can assess unfamiliar circumstances, identify what needs to change and retain practices that remain effective.','How does the writer define adaptability?','[{"label":"A","text":"Agreeing with every new workplace decision."},{"label":"B","text":"Responding thoughtfully while keeping useful existing practices."},{"label":"C","text":"Avoiding unfamiliar tasks whenever possible."},{"label":"D","text":"Changing established methods as frequently as possible."}]'::jsonb,'B','The writer presents adaptability as considered adjustment, not automatic acceptance of change.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-035','R01','B2','Education and Learning','Understanding an argument','ASSESSMENT POLICY DISCUSSION
Timed examinations can reveal how well students retrieve and organise knowledge under pressure. However, they offer only a partial picture of learning, particularly where a subject involves sustained research, collaboration or creative development. A broader assessment system would recognise these different forms of achievement.','What is the writer''s main position?','[{"label":"A","text":"Timed examinations should be removed from every subject."},{"label":"B","text":"Examinations measure all important learning outcomes."},{"label":"C","text":"Assessment should include evidence beyond timed examinations."},{"label":"D","text":"Creative work cannot be assessed fairly."}]'::jsonb,'C','The writer accepts the value of timed exams but argues that they do not capture every form of learning.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-036','R01','B2','Health and Nutrition','Understanding a qualification','PUBLIC HEALTH ARTICLE
Nutrition labels can help consumers compare products, but the information is useful only when interpreted in context. A single figure rarely tells the whole story: serving sizes differ, and dietary needs vary. The article therefore recommends using labels as one source of guidance rather than as a complete judgement of a product''s value.','What limitation of nutrition labels is emphasised?','[{"label":"A","text":"They provide no useful information to consumers."},{"label":"B","text":"They should be interpreted alongside serving sizes and individual needs."},{"label":"C","text":"They are designed only for people with medical conditions."},{"label":"D","text":"They make all products easy to compare."}]'::jsonb,'B','The article explains that figures need context because serving sizes and individual needs vary.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-037','R01','B2','Transportation and Travel','Understanding implication','PUBLIC TRANSPORT CONSULTATION
The proposed express route would reduce journey times for passengers travelling between the outer districts and the city centre. It would, however, bypass several residential areas currently served by local buses. The authority is therefore considering whether additional feeder services would be needed to prevent some communities from becoming less accessible.','What concern does the authority need to address?','[{"label":"A","text":"Whether the express route can use newer vehicles."},{"label":"B","text":"Whether journey times will increase for all passengers."},{"label":"C","text":"Whether residents in bypassed areas will retain convenient access."},{"label":"D","text":"Whether local buses should be removed from the city centre."}]'::jsonb,'C','The text raises the risk that communities bypassed by the express route may lose accessibility.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-038','R01','B2','Cities and Housing','Understanding purpose','TENANTS'' ASSOCIATION LETTER
We welcome the proposed improvements to the shared garden. Before work begins, however, residents would like clarification about how access will be maintained for people with limited mobility. A plan that improves the space for some tenants should not unintentionally make it harder for others to use.','What is the main purpose of the letter?','[{"label":"A","text":"To oppose all changes to the garden."},{"label":"B","text":"To request that accessibility be considered in the improvement plan."},{"label":"C","text":"To ask residents to stop using the garden."},{"label":"D","text":"To demand that the work be completed immediately."}]'::jsonb,'B','The association supports improvements but asks that access for people with limited mobility is protected.','core',80,'draft'),
('B2-039','R01','B2','Sports and Health','Understanding a contrast','SPORTS SCIENCE COMMENTARY
Wearable devices have made it easier for recreational athletes to monitor training patterns. Nevertheless, the availability of more data does not automatically lead to better decisions. Without an understanding of what the measurements represent, users may respond to normal variation as though it were a warning sign.','What is the commentator warning against?','[{"label":"A","text":"Using any device to record exercise."},{"label":"B","text":"Assuming that more data automatically produces better decisions."},{"label":"C","text":"Comparing training patterns over time."},{"label":"D","text":"Learning what different measurements mean."}]'::jsonb,'B','The text warns that data without understanding can lead to poor interpretations.','core',80,'draft'),
('B2-040','R01','B2','Food Production','Understanding consequence','FOOD SUPPLY REPORT
Shorter supply chains can improve communication between growers and retailers, making it easier to respond to changes in demand. However, relying on a small number of nearby producers may leave retailers more exposed to local crop failures. The report suggests that resilience depends on balancing local relationships with a sufficiently varied supply network.','What risk is associated with relying on a small number of local producers?','[{"label":"A","text":"Retailers may become more vulnerable to local crop failures."},{"label":"B","text":"Growers will lose all contact with retailers."},{"label":"C","text":"Demand will become impossible to predict."},{"label":"D","text":"Food will always take longer to reach shops."}]'::jsonb,'A','The report identifies local crop failure as a risk when the supplier base is too narrow.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-041','R01','B2','Artificial Intelligence','Understanding stance','AI IN THE WORKPLACE
Automated systems can reduce repetitive tasks and help staff identify patterns in large datasets. Their recommendations, however, reflect the information and assumptions built into them. Organisations should therefore make it possible for employees to question outputs, especially when decisions affect people''s opportunities or access to services.','What principle does the writer support?','[{"label":"A","text":"Automated recommendations should never be questioned."},{"label":"B","text":"Employees should be able to challenge AI outputs in important decisions."},{"label":"C","text":"AI systems should make all workplace decisions independently."},{"label":"D","text":"Only technical staff need to understand automated systems."}]'::jsonb,'B','The writer argues for human scrutiny and the ability to question AI recommendations, particularly in consequential decisions.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-042','R01','B2','Climate and Weather','Understanding a qualification','CLIMATE COMMUNICATION
A record-breaking temperature in one location does not, by itself, establish a long-term climate trend. Equally, a cooler-than-usual week does not disprove one. Climate patterns are identified through evidence collected over extended periods and across wider areas, rather than isolated observations.','What distinction does the text make?','[{"label":"A","text":"Daily weather events and long-term climate patterns require different kinds of evidence."},{"label":"B","text":"Local temperatures are more reliable than regional records."},{"label":"C","text":"A single hot day proves a climate trend."},{"label":"D","text":"Cool periods are unrelated to weather observations."}]'::jsonb,'A','The text distinguishes isolated weather observations from longer-term climate evidence.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-043','R01','B2','Energy and Electricity','Understanding implication','BUILDING ENERGY REVIEW
The installation of motion-sensitive lighting reduced unnecessary use in corridors. Yet the review found that some lights remained on for longer than expected because sensors were poorly positioned. The report recommends checking how the technology works in each building before assuming that the same solution will deliver identical results everywhere.','What does the report imply?','[{"label":"A","text":"Technology should be selected and adjusted to suit local conditions."},{"label":"B","text":"Motion sensors always reduce energy use by the same amount."},{"label":"C","text":"Corridor lighting should be removed completely."},{"label":"D","text":"The installation was unsuccessful in every building."}]'::jsonb,'A','The report says sensor placement affects results, so solutions need to be assessed in context.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-044','R01','B2','Consumer Economics','Understanding a condition','SUBSCRIPTION TERMS
Subscribers may pause their membership once during each twelve-month period. A pause must be requested at least five working days before the next renewal date. Requests made after renewal will apply to the following period, and fees already charged are not refundable under this arrangement.','When will a late pause request take effect?','[{"label":"A","text":"Immediately, with the current fee returned."},{"label":"B","text":"Before the next renewal, regardless of notice."},{"label":"C","text":"During the period after the next one."},{"label":"D","text":"In the following membership period."}]'::jsonb,'D','The terms state that requests made after renewal apply to the following period.','core',85,'draft'),
('B2-045','R01','B2','Space Exploration','Understanding argument','SPACE RESEARCH EDITORIAL
Public discussion often frames space exploration and investment in urgent terrestrial needs as competing priorities. This comparison can be useful when examining budgets, but it overlooks the ways research can produce shared benefits over time. The more productive question may be how to evaluate those benefits transparently and weigh them against immediate demands.','What approach does the writer favour?','[{"label":"A","text":"Rejecting any comparison between public spending priorities."},{"label":"B","text":"Evaluating long-term benefits transparently alongside immediate needs."},{"label":"C","text":"Giving space research priority over all other spending."},{"label":"D","text":"Measuring research only by its short-term financial return."}]'::jsonb,'B','The writer supports weighing long-term research benefits transparently against immediate public needs.','core',85,'draft')
on conflict (question_code) do update set
 category=excluded.category, cefr_level=excluded.cefr_level, topic=excluded.topic,
 skill=excluded.skill, passage=excluded.passage, prompt=excluded.prompt,
 options=excluded.options, correct_option=excluded.correct_option,
 rationale=excluded.rationale, difficulty=excluded.difficulty,
 estimated_seconds=excluded.estimated_seconds, status=excluded.status, updated_at=now();
commit;
select cefr_level, count(*) as r01_total
from public.reading_question_bank
where category='R01' and cefr_level in ('A2','B1','B2')
group by cefr_level order by cefr_level;
